{
  "title": "Repeated prefixes give no ordered f69v match in three historical mansion lists",
  "program": "L4",
  "statement": "Across 56 circular alignments, shared prefixes longer than one EVA unit do not match the ordered Anklesaria, al-Tusi, or Henry Bate lists beyond the same-length permutation controls. The lowest combined primary p-value is 0.70675 before adjustment, and all six Holm-adjusted p-values are 1.0. The three clockwise scan-cued starts and the sensitivity that also fixes initial classes yield no positive score against both nulls. The chosen test detects 24/24 clean and 24/24 noisy synthetic prefix-preserving encodings of the same lists at p ≤ 0.01. The four consecutive Arabic entries sharing the three written letters سعد require a four-locus common three-unit prefix under direct grapheme substitution. Each of the 56 alignments conflicts with at least two clear units in both primary transliterations. The literal Justi Chapter II German print branches from the Greater Bundahishn list and contains consecutive Parviz entries. An exact repeated-label rule has no compatible adjacent pair in ZL or Takahashi, with one ambiguous pair in RF. The published 20 proposed Herrmann pairs are omitted in the source, leaving that proposal without a recoverable full mapping for this page.",
  "check": "Re-evaluate a specific historical roster only after registering its manuscript witness, exact chosen spellings, allowed segmentation, and a positional feature independent of the lexical match. For any proposal using abbreviations or unstable spellings, freeze that encoding in advance and measure its performance on independently generated positives and the same length-conditioned alignment nulls.",
  "on_path": false,
  "hard": true,
  "sources": {
